{
  "_about": [
    "The status-coverage contract between the gas_sponsor client (Drupal) and gas-sponsor-relayer.",
    "The same bytes are committed in each repository's tests. Change them in both or neither.",
    "GET /status carries one mark per network: chains[<chainId>].covered. It is JSON true or JSON false, and it is present on every network entry, including one that reads {\"error\":\"unreachable\"}.",
    "SponsorStatus::coversSafe(chainId, safe) is true only when that mark is exactly JSON true AND the fund is in groups or createdFunds for that chain. Every other case is false: a false mark, a missing mark, a mark of any other type, a chain id of 0 or below, a network that is not listed. A status with a wrong mark still parses.",
    "The mark has three states, read by SponsorStatus::coverage(chainId), and each query says which in mark: covered (exactly JSON true), not_covered (JSON false, a network that is not listed, or a chain id of 0 or below), not_said (a listed network whose mark is missing or not a JSON boolean). not_said is never not_covered: a site waits and retries on it and never offers anyone to pay the fee.",
    "Each case builds a status answer from base plus its own chains, groups and createdFunds. queries lists what coversSafe answers for each (chainId, safe), and the network's mark."
  ],
